The make_virtual refactor was not applied because the Roslyn refactor tool is not built. Since the Logger property is protected and set in the constructor, I cannot easily substitute a mock logger. I will write the test as is, using a derived test class that overrides the Logger property to provide a mock ILogger<ApplicationHost>. This will allow me to verify the LogError calls.

I will submit a test file with a test subclass of ApplicationHost that overrides Logger, and tests for the DI loop detection and the exception logging in CreateInstanceSafe. I will use Moq for mocking ILogger and PluginManager dependencies.

